        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Middle East Issued on: 31/03/2026 - 08:13 Multiple explosions rocked Tehran on Tuesday, with news agencies reporting power outages in parts of the Iranian capital. Reporting from Tehran, FRANCE 24’s Reza Sayah says residents have been hearing “airstrikes, followed by the unnerving sound of thundering explosions,\" he says, noting that airstrikes have been knocking out power in parts of Tehran since Sunday before authorities manage to restore electricity in some neighbourhoods. 'The Houthis hold serious cards' expert says, amid threats to choke off Red Sea passage 30/03/2026 Middle East Trump's options in Iran range from bad to worse 30/03/2026 Middle East Sir Westmacott challenges Trump rationale as war on Iran sparks 'serious' economic fallout worldwide 30/03/2026 Middle East Kyiv useful to US, Gulf at critical time: Drone interceptors 'more effective than Patriot missiles' 30/03/2026 Middle East While Trump vows Iran deal on the way, 'evidence points to another direction' 30/03/2026 Middle East South Lebanon: Locals remain as war rages on 30/03/2026 Middle East Ukraine signs defence agreements with Gulf Nations eager to fend off Iranian drones 30/03/2026 Middle East US not 'postured' for another Iraq 2003: Iran maintains vast, 'high-quality military capability' 30/03/2026 Middle East One Lebanese soldier killed, Israel expands buffer zone in southern Lebanon 30/03/2026 Middle East"
